\section{Returned fields}{
Each field with its type, its unit, and what \code{NA} means when it is \code{NA}.

\describe{
\item{\code{aligner_id}}{string; never \code{NA}. mzLib's PairwiseAligner.Id, naming the method and every parameter, e.g. global-affine;BLOSUM62;open=11;extend=1;end-gaps=free. Store it with any mapped position.}
\item{\code{matrix}}{string; never \code{NA}. The substitution matrix's name, always BLOSUM62: mzLib's default, the only one the wire offers.}
\item{\code{gap_open}}{int; in \strong{half-bits (BLOSUM62 score units)}; never \code{NA}. The gap-open cost the aligner used: the option's value, or mzLib's default when it was absent.}
\item{\code{gap_extend}}{int; in \strong{half-bits (BLOSUM62 score units)}; never \code{NA}. The gap-extension cost the aligner used.}
\item{\code{end_gaps}}{string; never \code{NA}. free or charged: the end-gap rule the aligner used.}
\item{\code{max_cells}}{int; in \strong{cells}; never \code{NA}. The table limit the aligner used.}
\item{\code{record_count}}{int; in \strong{pairs}; never \code{NA}. Rows: the input pairs.}
